          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Size on <strong class="text-white">CADR and air changes per hour</strong>, not on the room rating printed on the box. The quick version: <strong class="text-white">buy a dust CADR figure roughly equal to your room's square footage</strong>, then add 25 to 50 percent for a high ceiling.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then size for the speed you will actually use. A purifier rated for twice your room, running quietly on low, cleans the same air as a smaller one at maximum — and it is the one that stays switched on overnight, which is when it matters most.
          </p>
